The grade curriculum is the template: *"every Grade 8 class is taught these subjects, this many
times a week."* You write it once per grade, then apply it to all that grade's classes rather than
assigning subjects class by class.

**You need:** access to **Timetable → Grade Curriculum**, and classes that already have the right
grade set on them — see [Add a Class](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-class).

## Steps

1. Open **Timetable → Grade Curriculum**.
2. Pick the **grade** you are editing at the top.
3. For each subject the grade is taught, select **Add Subject** and fill in:
   - **Subject** — searchable; the list comes from **Timetable → Configuration → Subjects & Rules**.
   - **Lessons / week** — how many periods a week this subject gets. This is the number the
     generator tries to place.
   - **Max per day** — the ceiling on any single day. Leave blank to accept the default.
   - **Max consecutive** — how many may run back to back. Leave blank to accept the default.

   Blank is not zero. Blank means "use the default"; the row shows an **(override)** marker only
   where you have set something explicitly.
4. Optionally fill in the **Book List** — a free-text list of the grade's books, kept alongside the
   curriculum.
5. Select **Save Curriculum**. You should see **Curriculum saved successfully**.

## Pushing it down to the classes

Saving the curriculum does **not** by itself change any class. To do that:

1. Select **Apply to Grade *N***.
2. Read the confirmation. It tells you what will happen: *subject entries are created for all
   classes in that grade, and existing teacher assignments are not changed.*
3. Confirm. The result tells you how many entries were **created** and how many **updated**.

Because it never touches teacher assignments, applying again after a curriculum change is safe — it
adds and adjusts subjects without unpicking who teaches what.

## Editing an existing curriculum

Change the numbers in place and **Save Curriculum**, then **Apply to Grade** again to push the
change out. Removing a subject from the curriculum does not retroactively strip it from classes that
already have it; remove it in [Class Subjects](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-class-subjects) if you need
it gone.

## What to do next

[Assign teachers to those subjects](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-class-subjects), then
[generate the timetable](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-generate-timetable).
